@startuml
title Verification & Account Flow - Email/Phone Verify + Cross-Channel Contact Change (M3)

actor Person

participant "VerifyPage" as VP
participant "ContactChangePage" as CP
participant "VerifyGateway" as VG
participant "AccountGateway" as AG
participant "ApiClient" as AC
participant "ApiInterceptor" as AI
participant "AuthStore" as AS
database "Spring Boot /verify + /account" as API

note over Person, API
  All endpoints below require a valid JWT (ApiInterceptor adds
  the Bearer token). Cooldown (60s) and daily cap (5) violations
  both answer 429 with one generic backend message, so the client
  copy cannot promise a precise wait - it says "wait a while"
  (verified against the backend exception messages).
end note

== Verify a level (EMAIL first, then PHONE) ==
Person -> VP : open /verify (AuthGuard) or the shell's Verify link
VP -> VG : request(level)
VG -> AC : post<void>('/verify/request', {level})
AC -> API : POST /verify/request
alt 202 Accepted
  API --> AC : (empty body)
  VP --> Person : code-entry phase - 8-char code (EMAIL) or 6-digit OTP (PHONE)
  note over VP
    Dev senders log the code to the backend console ([DEV SMTP]/[DEV SMS]);
    smtp-pulse / Twilio deliver for real once .env credentials are set.
  end note
  Person -> VP : code
  VP -> VG : confirm(level, code)
  VG -> AC : post<void>('/verify/confirm', {level, code})
  AC -> API : POST /verify/confirm
  alt correct (200 empty)
    API --> AC : 200 (claim persisted backend-side)
    VP -> AS : addLevel(level)   ' optimistic - no GET /me to re-read claims
    VP --> Person : "your <channel> is verified" - the panel disappears
  else wrong/expired (400) or throttled (429)
    API --> AC : ErrorResponse (generic message)
    VP --> Person : generic "invalid or expired" copy - stay on the code phase
  end
else 409 AlreadyVerified
  API --> AC : conflict (no code is sent, no throttle consumed)
  VP -> AS : addLevel(level)     ' the server says the claim exists
  VP --> Person : info notice "already verified" - never an error banner
else 429 throttled
  API --> AC : too many requests (cooldown OR daily cap)
  VP --> Person : rate-limit copy, no auto-retry (resend = manual request again)
end

note over VP
  SMART_ID is never offered - the backend rejects it with 400 (stub in v1).
  Level state is SESSION-LOCAL: after a reload the page shows both buttons
  again (no GET /me in v1 - reported gap); the first request re-discovers a
  verified level via the 409 above and re-hides the panel.
end note

== Contact change: email -> SMS proof to the current phone (cross-channel) ==
Person -> CP : open /account (AuthGuard) -> Change email section
CP -> AG : requestEmailChange(newEmail)   ' lowercased client-side
AG -> AC : post<void>('/account/email-change/request', body)
AC -> API : POST /account/email-change/request
note over API
  backend sends the OTP to the CURRENT PHONE (SMS), NOT to the new
  email - stealing the mailbox alone cannot change the contact.
end note
API --> AC : 202 Accepted (empty - the backend never echoes the destination)
CP --> Person : "we sent an SMS code to the phone number on your account"
note over CP
  Copy names the CHANNEL only: without GET /me there is no masked
  "+372..." to truthfully show (md examples were aspirational - gap).
end note
Person -> CP : 6-digit code
CP -> AG : confirmEmailChange(code)
AG -> AC : post<void>('/account/email-change/confirm', {code})
AC -> API : POST /account/email-change/confirm
API --> AC : 200 OK
CP --> Person : success - shows the NEW email (known locally)
note over CP
  request 400 "same as current" -> "the new one must be different" copy;
  duplicate target 409 -> backend message inline; wrong/expired/no-pending
  code on confirm -> generic copy. Sessions are NOT revoked by a contact
  change (only a password reset revokes refresh tokens).
end note

== Contact change: phone -> email proof to the current address (cross-channel) ==
Person -> CP : /account -> Change phone section
CP -> AG : requestPhoneChange(newPhone)
AG -> AC : post<void>('/account/phone-change/request', body)
AC -> API : POST /account/phone-change/request
note over API
  backend sends the OTP to the CURRENT EMAIL - losing the SIM alone
  cannot re-route verification texts.
end note
API --> AC : 202 Accepted
CP --> Person : "we sent an email code to the email address on your account"
Person -> CP : 6-digit code
CP -> AG : confirmPhoneChange(code)
AG -> AC : post<void>('/account/phone-change/confirm', {code})
AC -> API : POST /account/phone-change/confirm
API --> AC : 200 OK
CP --> Person : success - shows the NEW phone

note over AS, CP
  M3 as-built: AuthStore.levels() is an optimistic mirror (confirm success or
  request-409 adds the level; login/logout/cleared session resets it). The
  account page never shows a server-truthful "current email/phone" before a
  change - candidate backend follow-up: GET /me (04-CONTEXT decision 3).
end note
@enduml
